{{Wireless adapter |brand=Cisco |model=AIR-RM3000AC |revision=-A-K9 |asin=B00DXTDOMQ;UK;, B00D4EMEK8;UK; |manuf_country= |is_manuf=No |availability= |fcc_date=04/25/2013 |fcc_id=LDK102086 |ic_id=2461B-102086 |if=Mini PCIe |if_bus_version= |if_connector_type= |form_factor=module for Cisco AP |vendor_id= |device_id= |subvendor_id= |subdevice_id= |chip1_brand=Broadcom |chip1_model=BCM43460 |ant_conn= |802dot11_protocols=abgn+ac |txchains=3 |rxchains=3 |sstreams=3 |accessible_UART=No |flags= |oui= |lin_driver= |win_driver= }} {{TagLine|Cisco Aironet 802.11ac Module (RM3000)}}
*Per the FCC photos, this device appears to be an expansion board :(w/ '''Altera''' PLD/FPGA) for a Mini PCIe (full-size) wireless module.
*The FCC test report indicates that the FCC ID also covers :the AIR-RM3000AC-N-K9 and AIR-RM3000AC-Z-K9.
:A label affixed to the device in the FCC sample label (reading ''BCM SROM 1203'') :shot as well as the correspondence letters indicate the device uses a [[Broadcom]] :chipset , likely BCM43460.
{{WiFiCert|WFA12320|07/29/2013}}
